course: dictionary
lesson: 14740
title: Words that show importance
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Prominently has two meanings, and the context tells you which one to use. Read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «The safety sign was displayed prominently at the pool gate.» A sign displayed prominently is put where everyone can see it easily, so prominently means easy to see or notice.
explain: «She figures prominently in the story.» There is no sign here. The clue is the word story: someone who figures prominently plays a big, important part in it. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Prominently is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done. It often comes after words like displayed, placed, featured or figured. Ask yourself: is the thing easy to see, or is it important? That question will lead you to the right meaning.
fact: Prominently is an adverb. It tells you how something is done.
fact: «Prominently» means in a place or way that is easy to see or notice.
fact: «Prominently» can also mean in an important way, playing a big part.
fact: «Feature prominently» and «figure prominently» are common phrases: a thing that features prominently is clearly important.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The rules were displayed prominently on the wall.» What does prominently mean here? | *In a place where everyone can easily see them | Very late at night | Quietly, in a whisper | Only for a short time
exercise: «Her name figures prominently in the history book.» What does prominently mean here? | Far away from the rest of the book | *In an important way, playing a big part | Without any pictures | Written in very small letters
exercise: «The red stop sign stood prominently on the corner.» Find and copy the word that tells you how the sign stood. | corner | red | stop | *prominently
test: «The new library featured prominently in the town's plans.» What does featured prominently suggest? | It was forgotten by everyone | It was painted bright yellow | *It was an important part of the plans | It was hidden away from view
test: Ben says prominently means quietly. Why is he wrong? | Because prominently means late | Because prominently means quietly | *Because prominently means easy to see, or important | Because prominently is a noun
exam: «The lighthouse stands prominently on the cliff, so ships can see it from far away.» What does prominently mean here? | Hidden behind the trees | Very quietly | *Easy to see from far away | Slowly, one step at a time
